// ===========================================================================
// 51-aquarius-game-mode.rules — who may switch to Game Mode, and who may not
// ===========================================================================
// PLAIN ENGLISH
//
// This narrows the one privileged job AquariusOS adds for Game Mode
// (org.aquariusos.gamemode.select, described in
// /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.aquariusos.gamemode.policy) down to the only
// person who should ever be able to do it: somebody sitting at this computer,
// in the session that owns the screen right now, who is an administrator.
//
// ⚠️ AND FOR THAT ONE PERSON IT IS ALLOWED WITH NO PASSWORD. That is on
// purpose and it is the only place on this computer where we do it. The switch
// is pressed from the sofa with a controller in your hands, and a password box
// cannot be typed into with a controller. The policy file above works through
// what is and is not being risked; the short version is that this person can
// already end their own session, and all this lets them do is choose what
// starts next.
//
// Everybody else — over SSH, from a session that has been switched away from,
// from an account that is not an administrator, from any program running as
// anyone else — gets a flat no, and no box appears at all. `subject.active`
// is the part that means "the session that owns the screen right now": it is
// false the moment the screen belongs to somebody else, which is exactly when
// this must not work.
//
// ⚠️ THIS FILE MUST NEVER BE WIDENED TO COVER ANYTHING ELSE. It names one
// action id and returns NOT_HANDLED for every other question, so it cannot
// accidentally grant something else no-password rights. If a future feature
// needs a privileged job, it gets its own action and its own rule, and it
// almost certainly gets a password prompt rather than this.
// ===========================================================================

polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (action.id != "org.aquariusos.gamemode.select") {
        return polkit.Result.NOT_HANDLED;
    }

    // The person at the screen, in the session that owns it, who is an
    // administrator: yes, straight away, no password.
    if (subject.active && subject.local && subject.isInGroup("wheel")) {
        return polkit.Result.YES;
    }

    // Anybody else: no, and do not even ask.
    return polkit.Result.NO;
});
